# G-Code Community License 1.0

## 1. Acceptance

O-Research ("we", "us") makes G-Code (the "software") available under these terms. "You" means the person or organization that gets the software. By using, copying, changing or sharing the software, you accept these terms. If you do not accept them, you have no permission to do any of those things.

## 2. Free use

You may use, copy and change the software free of charge if you are one of these:

(a) **An individual** using it on your own behalf, for any purpose, including paid work. This covers personal projects, study, research, freelance and self-employed work, work you deliver to clients, and selling what you make with the software. A company whose only person using the software is its owner counts as an individual.

(b) **A student, teacher, school, college or university** using it for teaching, learning or non-commercial academic research.

(c) **A non-profit organization recognized as charitable where it is based**, using it for its charitable work.

## 3. Organizations pay per seat

Any other use by or for an organization needs a paid commercial license from us, with one seat for each person who uses the software. An organization is a company, partnership, government body, or any other group or legal entity. Use for an organization includes use by its employees in their work, and use by anyone the organization provides the software to or directs to use it. The price and terms of a seat are in `COMMERCIAL.md`.

An outside contractor who chooses and runs their own copy in their own independent business is using it under 2(a), unless the organization provides the software or directs its use.

An organization may try the software for 30 days before buying seats.

## 4. Limits for everyone

Whether you use the software free or with seats, you may not, without our written permission:

(a) sell, rent, lease or sublicense the software or a changed version of it, or charge for access to it, including by offering it as a hosted or managed service;

(b) build a business on the software: offer, for money or through a company you run, a product or service that is the software, a changed version of it, or a work that contains a substantial part of its source code;

(c) remove or change the Required Notice, these terms, or the license notices of third-party parts.

Using the software as a tool to make other things is not limited by this section.

## 5. What you make with the software

These terms do not cover what you create with the software. Code, text and other output you make with G-Code are yours, subject to your agreements with others (such as the terms of any model provider you connect), and you may use them for any purpose.

## 6. Changes and sharing

You may change the software for any use these terms allow. A changed version stays under these terms.

You may share copies of the software, changed or not, free of charge, if:

- everyone who gets a copy from you also gets these terms and the Required Notice;
- a changed version says prominently that it was changed, and by whom;
- you do not present a changed version as the official G-Code, or as made or endorsed by us.

People who get a copy from you get their permissions from us, under these terms, not from you.

